WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.100
There are plenty of examples of what not to do in a lot of these films.

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:09.230
*epic inspirational trumpet*

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:17.020
*hissing*

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:20.290
In my line of work you run into snakes fairly often

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:27.060
And you do have to be careful. You know snakes will come cruising through an archeological site and some people freak out, and I run after it and catch it.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.730
And come back and freak people out a little more. 

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:42.230
A lot of the destruction of antiquities that happens in many of the different films is something that we really try to avoid. 

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:48.180
He is not patient. He's not patient at all and archeology is a science of incredible patience. 

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:52.890
The opening of the Ark of the Covenant is not something you would do lightly. 

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.560
So that's very impatient. 

00:01:00.270 --> 00:01:05.600
I know people who have had to shoot it out with bandits. Who've had graduate students kidnapped. 

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:11.960
I know people who have been kidnapped and assaulted, and when they start shooting you shoot back.

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:16.880
Nothing shocks me. I'm a scientist. 

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:24.460
There is kind of rush that you get when you're holding an artifact that no ones seen or touched in thousands of years. It is quite thrilling. 

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:34.710
I was a little let down by Kingdom of the Crystal Skull. First of all there are no known civilizations like that in South America. 

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:39.630
A lot of the crystal skulls that we know of appear to have been manufactured in the modern era. 

00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:48.040
The first one is the best in the series, I think. I like the third one too. And hopefully number five will be even better. 

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:52.340
*epic inspiring trumpet*

